            "character": "它",
            "pinyin": "tā",
            "meaning": "it",
            "audio_text": "它"
          }
        ]
      },
      "notice": "All three are tā. In speech there is no difference at all.",
      "discover": "他 is written for he, 她 for she, 它 for an animal or a thing. The distinction exists only on the page — hearing tā tells you nothing about which character was meant.",
